  "job_B1.4.5_20251001_193240": {
    "text": "Se godspellere Iohannes s\u00e6de on \u00feysum godspelle \u00fe\u00e6t Crist ure H\u00e6lend, \u00fea \u00fea he her on life w\u00e6s, come\nSe H\u00e6lend \u00fea s\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r, of \u00f0am si\u00f0f\u00e6te werig, wi\u00f0 \u00f0one w\u00e6terpytt, and hit w\u00e6s \u00fea midd\u00e6g, and his\n\u00dea com \u00fe\u00e6r betwux \u00feam of Samarian byrig an wif to \u00f0am w\u00e6terscipe, wolde w\u00e6ter feccan, and se\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to andsware, Hwi wilt \u00feu me \u00fe\u00e6s biddan, \u00feonne \u00feu eart Iudeisc, and ic Samaritanisc\nNella\u00f0 \u00fea Iudeiscan mid nanum Samaritaniscum etan o\u00f0\u00f0e drincan.\nHyre andwyrde se H\u00e6lend, Gyf \u00feu cu\u00feest Godes gyfe, and wistest hwa \u00fee cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Syle me drincan,\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to, \u00fees w\u00e6terpyt ys deop, and \u00feu hl\u00e6df\u00e6t n\u00e6fst; hwanon h\u00e6fst \u00feu liflic w\u00e6ter?\nEart \u00feu la fur\u00f0or \u00feonne ure f\u00e6der Iacob, \u00fee us \u00feysne pyt forgeaf?\nAnd he sylf \u00fe\u00e6rof dranc, and hys bearn and nytenu.\nHyre andwyrde se H\u00e6lend, \u00e6lcum \u00fe\u00e6ra \u00feyrst eft \u00fee of \u00feysum w\u00e6tere drinc\u00f0, and \u00feam ne \u00feyrst on\nHim andwyrde \u00fe\u00e6t wif, Hlaford, syle me of \u00feysum liflican w\u00e6tere, \u00fe\u00e6t me heonon for\u00f0 ne \u00feyrste, ne ic\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend hyre to, Gang clypa \u00feinne wer, and cum hider \u00feonne.\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to andsware, N\u00e6bbe ic nanne wer.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend, Wel \u00feu cw\u00e6de, wif, n\u00e6bbe ic nanne wer; fif weras \u00feu h\u00e6fdest, and \u00feone \u00fee \u00feu nu\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to, Hlaford, ic geseo \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu witega eart; and ure f\u00e6deras woldon on \u00feysum\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend hyre to, Wif, gelif \u00feu me \u00fe\u00e6t se tima cym\u00f0 \u00feonne ge eow ne gebidda\u00f0 ne on\nGod so\u00f0lice is gast, and \u00feam \u00f0e him to gebidda\u00f0 gedafena\u00f0 to gebiddanne on gaste and on\n\u00de\u00e6t wif him cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to, Ic wat \u00fe\u00e6t us cym\u00f0 se \u00f0e is gehaten M\u00e6ssias, \u00fe\u00e6t is H\u00e6lend Crist, and \u00feonne\nHyre andwyrde se H\u00e6lend, Ic hit eom \u00fee \u00fee to sprece.\nMid \u00feam \u00fea comon Cristes leorningcnihtas, and hi wundrodon \u00fe\u00e6t he to wifmenn spr\u00e6c; heora nan\n\u00de\u00e6t wif \u00fea forlet hyre w\u00e6terf\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r, and eode into \u00f0\u00e6re byrig, and to \u00f0am burhwarum cw\u00e6\u00f0, Cuma\u00f0\nAnd seo burhwaru \u00fea eode ut ardlice to him.\n\u00dea b\u00e6don his leorningcnihtas hine betwux \u00feam, cwe\u00feende, Ett, leof lareow.\nAnd he him andwyrde \u00feus: Ic h\u00e6bbe mete to etenne \u00feone \u00fee ge nyton.\nHys discipuli \u00fea s\u00e6don digellice him betwynan, Hw\u00e6\u00f0er \u00e6nig man him brohte mete hider?\nSe H\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea to, Min mete is so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fe\u00e6s willan wyrce \u00fee me hider asende \u00fe\u00e6t ic hys\nLa hu ne secge ge \u00fe\u00e6t feower mon\u00f0as synt gyt \u00e6r \u00feam \u00fee gerip cume?\nEfne ic secge eow, sceawia\u00f0 \u00feas eardas, for \u00f0am \u00fee hi synd gearwe to geripe nu, and se \u00fee rip\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t\nOn \u00feam is so\u00f0 word gecw\u00e6den, \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00f0er is se \u00f0e s\u00e6w\u00f0 and o\u00f0er se \u00f0e rip\u00f0.\nIc sende eow to rippanne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t ge ne beswuncon; o\u00f0re hit beswuncon, and ge ferdon in to heora\nOf \u00fe\u00e6re burhware \u00fea Samarian byrig manega menn gelyfdon on \u00feone lifigendan H\u00e6lend for \u00f0\u00e6s wifes\n\u00dea \u00fea seo burhwaru him com to, \u00fea b\u00e6don hi hine georne \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fe\u00e6r wunode, and he wunode \u00fe\u00e6r\nLangsum trahtnung belimp\u00f0 to \u00f0ysum godspelle, and ge ne magon undergytan ealle \u00fea deopnysse\nSe h\u00e6lend w\u00e6s werig, \u00feeah \u00fee hit wundorlic si.\nHis heofonlica F\u00e6der \u00feurh hine gesceop ealle gesceafta buton geswince; ne swanc se F\u00e6der ne se\nOn \u00fe\u00e6re sixtan tide he s\u00e6t werig \u00e6t \u00feam pytte, and on \u00f0\u00e6re syxtan ylde \u00feysre worulde he com to\n\u00de\u00e6r com of Samarian byrig, swa swa we s\u00e6don eow \u00e6r, \u00fe\u00e6t wif to \u00feam H\u00e6lende, and heo h\u00e6fde\nSe H\u00e6lend b\u00e6d drincan, swa swa ge gehyrdon \u00e6r, \u00e6t \u00feam Samaritaniscan wife, for \u00f0an \u00f0e he\n\u00dea wundrode \u00fe\u00e6t wif \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde drincan of hyre f\u00e6te, for \u00f0am \u00f0e \u00fea Iudeiscan noldon n\u00e6fre brucan\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam wife, gyf \u00feu cu\u00feest Godes gyfe; Godes gyfu is se Halga Gast; so\u00f0lice \u00feone Gast\nAnd he cw\u00e6\u00f0 be \u00feam w\u00e6tere \u00fee w\u00e6s on \u00feam pytte, \u00c6lcum \u00fe\u00e6ra \u00feyrst eft \u00fee of \u00feysum w\u00e6tere drinc\u00f0,\nSe \u00f0e gelyf\u00f0 on me, swa swa gewritu secga\u00f0, of his inno\u00f0e flowa\u00f0 liflices w\u00e6teres flod; \u00feis s\u00e6de se\nHe is se liflica wylspring, and \u00feam \u00f0e he on wuna\u00f0 ne \u00feyrst on ecnysse, ac \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif him bi\u00f0\n\u00de\u00e6t wif nyste \u00fea gyt hwilc w\u00e6ter he m\u00e6nde, and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Hlafurd, syle me drincan of \u00feysum liflican\nHeo wolde \u00fea iu beon buton geswince, ac heo ne gehyrde \u00fea gyt hw\u00e6t se H\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0 on sumre o\u00f0re\nGe ne magon understandan \u00fea micclan deopnysse ealles \u00feyses godspelles, swa swa we \u00e6r s\u00e6don, and\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00f0am wife, Wif, gelyf \u00feu me \u00fe\u00e6t se tima cym\u00f0 \u00feonne ge eow ne gebidda\u00f0 ne on \u00feysum\nAc se tima cym\u00f0, and nu is so\u00f0lice, \u00feonne \u00fea so\u00f0an biddendras gebidda\u00f0 hi to \u00f0am F\u00e6der on gaste\nGod so\u00f0lice is gast, and \u00feam \u00f0e him to gebidda\u00f0 gedafena\u00f0 to gebiddenne on gaste and on\nNu ne \u00feurfe we astigan to sticolum muntum mid earfo\u00f0nysse, us to gebiddanne, swilce God si\nSe heaga munt getacna\u00f0 \u00fea heagan modignysse, and seo dene eadmodnysse, \u00fee ure Drihten lufa\u00f0, and\nNe we ne \u00feurfon secan ofer s\u00e6 ne ofer land, mid widgilre worunge, \u00feone welwillendan God, \u00feone \u00fee\nWitodlice \u00fea Iudeiscan \u00fee \u00fea wur\u00feedon God geb\u00e6don hi to Gode binnan \u00feam temple, and Crist cw\u00e6\u00f0\nSe h\u00e6l ys so\u00f0lice ure H\u00e6lend Crist, se \u00f0e of Iudeiscum cynne com of Marian, \u00fee w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00deyss wiston \u00fea witegan \u00fee hit witegodon toweard, and of \u00feam cynne comon Cristes apostoli, and\n\u00de\u00e6t wif cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Criste, Ic wat \u00fe\u00e6t M\u00e6ssias cym\u00f0, se \u00f0e ys Crist gecweden; and he cw\u00e6\u00f0 to hire, Ic\nMessias on Ebreisc, Christus on Grecisc, unctus on Leden, ys on Englisc gesmyrod; \u00fe\u00e6t ys ure\n\u00de\u00e6t wif forlet \u00fea sona hyre w\u00e6terf\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6r standan, and efste to \u00f0\u00e6re byrig and bodade ymbe crist.\nMid \u00feam \u00fee heo gehyrde of \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes mu\u00fee, Ic hit eom, se \u00f0e to \u00f0e sprece, \u00fea efste heo swi\u00f0e\nHeo forlet hyre w\u00e6terf\u00e6t, \u00fee h\u00e6fde getacnunge woruldlicre gewilnunge, and wear\u00f0 \u00fea bydel, and\n\u00dea b\u00e6don his leorningcnihtas hine betwux \u00feam, \u00feus cwe\u00feende: Ett, leof lareow; and he him andwyrde\nHer ge magon gehyran \u00fe\u00e6t ure H\u00e6lend \u00e6t, \u00feonne his leorningcnihtas hine la\u00f0edon to mete, \u00feeah \u00fee\nHe ne cu\u00f0e na \u00fea Cristes boc \u00fee us cy\u00f0 ymbe \u00fe\u00e6t, \u00fe\u00e6t ure H\u00e6lend \u00e6te swa swa o\u00f0re men do\u00f0, ge \u00e6r\nHe \u00e6t so\u00f0lice and dranc, for \u00f0am \u00f0e he so\u00f0 man w\u00e6s; he \u00e6t buton gyfernysse and dranc buton\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min mete is \u00fe\u00e6t ic \u00fe\u00e6s willan wyrce \u00fee me hider asende \u00fe\u00e6t ic his weorc gefylle.\nHys gastlica mete ys mancynnes alysednyss, and him \u00feyrste on \u00feam wife hyre geleafan, and he\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic secge eow, sceawia\u00f0 \u00feas eardas, for \u00f0am \u00f0e hi synd gearwe to geripe nu, and se \u00f0e rip\u00f0\nOn \u00feam is so\u00f0 word gecweden, \u00fe\u00e6t o\u00feer is se \u00f0e s\u00e6w\u00f0, and o\u00f0er se \u00f0e rip\u00f0; ic sende eow to ripanne\n\u00dea heahf\u00e6deras and \u00fea witegan \u00fee embe \u00feone H\u00e6lend cyddon, \u00fea w\u00e6ron \u00fea s\u00e6deras \u00fee seowon\nSo\u00f0lice ure H\u00e6lend \u00feurh hine sylfne eft and \u00feurh his apostolas and heora \u00e6ftergengan seow \u00fea\nEnglas beo\u00f0 \u00fea rifteras_ \u00fea rifteras on ende \u00feysre worulde, swa swa Crist sylf s\u00e6de on sumon his\n\u00deonne scina\u00f0 \u00fea rihtwisan, swa swa sunne de\u00f0 nu, on heora F\u00e6der rice; \u00feis s\u00e6de se H\u00e6lend.\nSeo burhwaru gelyfde, swa swa we s\u00e6don \u00e6r, \u00e6rest \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t wif; and eft, \u00fea \u00fea hi comon to Criste\nOn \u00feone we eac gelyfa\u00f0, se \u00f0e alysde us.\nSi him wuldor and lof a to worulde, amen.",
